Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:46:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] U16 review: verse references load only where a page asks
 for them

Markdown.tsx and Prose imported VerseRef statically, so every Markdown or
Prose page (essays, books, care pages, history and nation essays) loaded
the verse sheet, Radix (vendor-ui, 11 KB gzip), and the book table (about
18 KB gzip in all) without using any of it. The remark plugin moves to
MarkdownVerseRefs.tsx, loaded lazily by Markdown only with verseRefs, and
Prose loads RefText the same way; until it arrives the text reads as
plain prose. A built essay page now requests none of it.

The too-long sheet now counts chapters ("Psalms 1; 23; 91; 139" covers 4
chapters) instead of naming the first and last as a range. The
.st-verseref block moves beside the Sheet rules so it no longer lands at
the line U17 also appends to.

